{{also|postmortem|post-mortem|post mórtem}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|postmortem|post-mortem}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mer-|id=die}}
From {{bor|en|la|post||afterwards}} + {{m|la|mortem}}, from {{m|la|mors||death}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|head=post mortem}}

# Having been [[inflict|inflicted]] or having occurred after [[death]].
#: {{ux|en|We shouldn't let these '''post mortem''' injuries distract us while looking for the cause of death.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''post mortem''' timeline is incomplete.}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|antemortem}}
* {{l|en|premortem}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|perimortem}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-|head=post mortem}}

# Occurring after death.
#: {{ux|en|The injuries were found to have been caused '''post mortem'''.}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|antemortem}}
* {{l|en|premortem}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|perimortem}}

