===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=post mortem}}

# An [[investigation]] of a [[corpse]] to determine the cause of [[death]].
#: {{syn|en|autopsy|PM}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|management}} Any investigation after the conclusion of an activity, particularly when said activity produces an unwanted outcome.
#: {{syn|en|debriefing|AAR}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2014-09-03|author=[[w:Tom Limoncelli|Thomas A. Limoncelli]]|author2=Strata R. Chalup|author3=Christina J. Hogan|series=Designing and Operating Large Distributed Systems|seriesvolume=2|publisher=Addison-Wesley|title=The Practice of Cloud System Administration|page=300|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=RY1pBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA300|text=Each user-visible outage or SLA violation should be followed by a '''postmortem''' and conclude with implementation of the recommendations in the '''postmortem''' report.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|month=October|author=Ian Walmsley|title=Cleaning up|journal=Modern Railways|page=44|text=After a serious delay there is often a '''post mortem''' on what happened, but this is usually in-house.}}

